# earlier names claimed more than they proved. Each removes the post-sample
# admission guard, not the sequential split that feeds it. That is deliberate:
# with the guard gone the split has no observable consequence here. It exists
# only so the guard has a measurement to use, and this harness charges tokens
# when an agent is INVOKED and never makes agent() throw past the target — the
# one place a collapsed wave would otherwise differ, by losing the agents it
# launched past the ceiling. A mutant that also collapsed the split would
# therefore be killed by the same assertion, for the same reason, and naming
# it after the split would be the overstatement this file exists to avoid.
#
# KNOWN-EQUIVALENT, excluded deliberately rather than left to survive:
#
#   escrow draw token gate          (admitTokens inside drawOrReserve)

#
# Three others used to sit here on the strength of absorb() sorting each
# finder's candidates. That argument was wrong: absorb sorts each finder's OWN
# list, which leaves the concatenated array in finder-processing order — and
# that is exactly where a selector with no content tie-break falls back to
# "whoever answered first". They are live mutants again, killed by scenarios
# that swap which lens filed which claim.
#
# The escrow one needs two cases, not the one the note used to claim. It is
# NOT true that every draw is re-checked at launch: the first item of a
# multi-item wave is the sample, and the sample launches without one.
#   - Escrow covers exactly one item, so in a multi-item wave the second
#     comes from reserve(), whose admitTokens sees waveEstimateWU already
#     carrying the first. If the second is admitted the first would have
#     been; if it is refused the wave has one item, which is the next case.
#   - A one-item wave has no sample, so its single item IS re-checked after
#     endWave, by the same admitTokens the mutant removed.
# Either way the removed check is asked again before anything launches.
#
# It is kept as defence in depth — it is what would still be right if the
# launch-time re-check were removed — but a mutant for it would survive by
# construction, and a suite that tolerates a silent survivor is the thing this
# file exists to prevent.

